CS35L41 subsystem ID: pick the Halo protection firmware linux-firmware keys by
this board's amplifier subsystem ID.

The generic cirrus/cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot.wmfw (v0.58.0) that the driver falls
back to when it cannot name the amplifier does not carry the MAX_LRCLK_DELAY /
CAL_R / CAL_CHECKSUM / CAL_STATUS controls the protection bring-up in 0004
writes, so the amplifier DSP never starts:

    snd-sc8280xp sound: ASoC: POST_PMU: TL DSP1 event failed: -2        (ENOENT)
    snd-sc8280xp sound: ASoC: POST_PMU: TL Main AMP event failed: -13   (gate)

and the playback stream blocks forever.  linux-firmware already ships the
matching build keyed by this board's subsystem ID
(cirrus/cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot-10251826.wmfw -> cs35l41/v6.83.0/
halo_cspl_RAM_revB2_29.85.0.wmfw), so naming the four amplifiers is enough.
Measured before/after on the unit: the generic build logs "Subsystem ID not
found" and the DSP1/Main AMP events above; with the property the same boot
loads the 10251826 keyed firmware.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -2293,3 +2293,17 @@
 	data-lanes = <0 1>;
 };
 
+
+/*
+ * linux-firmware keys this board's CS35L41 Halo protection firmware on the
+ * amplifier subsystem ID.  Without the property the driver logs "Subsystem ID
+ * not found" and falls back to the generic cirrus/cs35l41-dsp1-spk-prot.wmfw,
+ * which does not carry the MAX_LRCLK_DELAY / CAL_* controls the protection
+ * bring-up (0004) writes; the amp DSP then fails to start (POST_PMU: * DSP1
+ * event failed: -2) and the amplifier gate never opens.  10251826 is the ID
+ * linux-firmware's own cirrus files are keyed by for this board.
+ */
+&cs35l41_tl { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+&cs35l41_tr { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+&cs35l41_br { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
+&cs35l41_bl { cirrus,subsystem-id = "10251826"; };
